# Maintenance Mode
#
# To enable maintenance mode, copy this file to `.maintenance` (in this same directory)
#
# Then edit `.maintenance` and replace `my-secret-key` with a random secret and delete
# everything else -- only the plain text string of the bypass
# The file must contain a single line: the bypass key.
#
# What it does:
#   - Every page will return HTTP 503 with a standalone maintenance page.
#   - Search engines receive a Retry-After header (1 hour).
#   - The site is completely inaccessible to visitors.
#
# Bypass (admin access):
#   Visit any page with ?bypass=<secret-key> (e.g. https://www.savpdfviewer.com/?bypass=<secret-key>).
#   A cookie is set for 24 hours, and all pages load normally with a yellow
#   "MAINTENANCE MODE ACTIVE" banner at the top.
#
# To deactivate:
#   Delete the `.maintenance` file
#
#   The site returns to normal immediately. No restart needed.
#
# Note: `.maintenance` is listed in .gitignore and will not be committed.
